  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116446",
      "title": "Activated Route vs Activated Route Snapshot",
      "lectureOrder": 285,
      "videoOrder": 272,
      "sourceHash": "3c8668067ef296a55801bf1a6d2e4853a4e984d20b36769ef7e7d7cb6792bb5b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.51,
          "end": 4.35,
          "en": "So at this point, you already learned a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.35,
          "end": 8.04,
          "en": "about Angular's router and routing mechanism,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.04,
          "end": 11.64,
          "en": "and we will indeed also dive even deeper than that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.64,
          "end": 14.34,
          "en": "throughout the rest of this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.34,
          "end": 16.41,
          "en": "But first, I wanna come back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.41,
          "end": 19.83,
          "en": "to this activatedRoute object here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.83,
          "end": 22.26,
          "en": "which you could inject into your Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.26,
          "end": 24.96,
          "en": "to get access to some information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.96,
          "end": 29.07,
          "en": "about the activatedRoute, like the route parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.07,
          "end": 32.31,
          "en": "And as you learned, this gives you an alternative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.31,
          "end": 36.03,
          "en": "to relying on Angular's input mechanism",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.03,
          "end": 39.99,
          "en": "where it can also provide route parameters as inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.99,
          "end": 41.103,
          "en": "if enabled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.21,
          "end": 44.07,
          "en": "You learned about this approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.07,
          "end": 47.1,
          "en": "and this activatedRoute object indeed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.1,
          "end": 49.74,
          "en": "also provides some other information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.74,
          "end": 53.04,
          "en": "You can, for example, also use it to extract information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.04,
          "end": 54.69,
          "en": "about query parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.69,
          "end": 58.86,
          "en": "or about data that might have been set or loaded up front,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.86,
          "end": 61.32,
          "en": "but I'll get back to that later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.32,
          "end": 65.07,
          "en": "Instead, what I want to focus on here in this lecture",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.07,
          "end": 68.28,
          "en": "is that this activatedRoute object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.28,
          "end": 71.22,
          "en": "does not just have these properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.22,
          "end": 74.61,
          "en": "that can be used to set up subscriptions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.61,
          "end": 79.53,
          "en": "but instead, you can also access a snapshot property on it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.53,
          "end": 82.28999999999999,
          "en": "And that then gives you an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.28999999999999,
          "end": 86.67,
          "en": "which seemingly has basically the same properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.67,
          "end": 90.003,
          "en": "as the activatedRoute, for example, a paramMap.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.02,
          "end": 93.81,
          "en": "But there is one super important difference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.81,
          "end": 97.593,
          "en": "between the snapshot and the activatedRoute as a whole.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.43,
          "end": 102.99000000000001,
          "en": "Because if you log that snapshot here and you visit a user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.99000000000001,
          "end": 106.44,
          "en": "you will see that it looks the same on first sight,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.44,
          "end": 109.11,
          "en": "but all the values you're dealing with here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.11,
          "end": 113.00999999999999,
          "en": "are now not subjects or observables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.00999999999999,
          "end": 117.63300000000001,
          "en": "but instead actual values that you could use like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 118.77000000000001,
          "end": 123.03,
          "en": "For example, if you want to use the user ID parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 123.03,
          "end": 125.23,
          "en": "you could get it from the paramMap",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 126.96,
          "end": 129.99,
          "en": "or through the params object here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 129.99,
          "end": 132.42,
          "en": "this nested params object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.42,
          "end": 136.38,
          "en": "So you could get the user ID here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 136.38,
          "end": 140.97,
          "en": "by accessing activatedRoute.snapshot.paramMap,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.97,
          "end": 145.35,
          "en": "and then get the user ID like we did it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 145.35,
          "end": 147.633,
          "en": "but now based on this snapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.65,
          "end": 150.96,
          "en": "But the downside of this approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 150.96,
          "end": 155.19,
          "en": "is now that this is now not a reactive object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 155.19,
          "end": 156.93,
          "en": "or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 156.93,
          "end": 159.42000000000002,
          "en": "Instead the user ID gets logged here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.42000000000002,
          "end": 161.67000000000002,
          "en": "but as you now switch users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 161.67000000000002,
          "end": 163.953,
          "en": "this log never gets updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 164.85,
          "end": 168.36,
          "en": "So this now is not re-executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 168.36,
          "end": 173.36,
          "en": "as the Component changes because ngOnInit isn't re-executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 173.73,
          "end": 176.79,
          "en": "That's why we set up a subscription earlier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 176.79,
          "end": 178.53,
          "en": "But if you have a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.53,
          "end": 182.82,
          "en": "where you know that it doesn't need to be re-executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 182.82,
          "end": 185.34,
          "en": "so if you have a use case that's different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 185.34,
          "end": 187.92,
          "en": "from the one we have in this demo app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 187.92,
          "end": 191.46,
          "en": "then you could indeed use this snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 191.46,
          "end": 193.5,
          "en": "to get quick and easy access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.5,
          "end": 196.56,
          "en": "to some route data like these parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 196.56,
          "end": 198.12,
          "en": "But if you're on a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 198.12,
          "end": 202.29,
          "en": "that indeed is reused as your route might change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.29,
          "end": 205.26,
          "en": "you should instead rely on subscriptions like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 205.26,
          "end": 208.5,
          "en": "or on Angular's input mechanism.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 208.5,
          "end": 211.56,
          "en": "But that's just also something to be aware of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 211.56,
          "end": 215.31,
          "en": "because using this snapshot is also something you'll see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 215.31,
          "end": 216.723,
          "en": "in some projects.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
